Hi Christian,

Christian Brix Folsted Andersen wrote:
> I have both the files:
> 
> /proc/acpi/battery/state:
> /proc/acpi/battery/info:I

Both look good, as they should.

I've tried KDE 3.0.4 (part of SuSE Pro 8.1) on my Evo N160 and got the 
same weird message complaining about missing ACPI support. Unfortunately 
I don't know what you should try next. I could imagine the KDE power 
management tool uses another (fixed) directory name for the battery, the 
AC adapter etc. or something like that. There were similar problems 
discussed on this list in the past, but I didn't read them because I 
didn't use KDE.

I recommend you post another question about this problem on this list. 
This way I'm convinced you won't have to wait a long time until you get 
the information you need. You could also have a look at the list archive 
and try to find out if this issue has already been discussed here.

I'm sure you'll manage it ;-)

Regards
Heiko



